{
  "proposal": "SCOPE. Nothing was executed; every trace is by hand from the supplied code. No all-CNF bound is claimed.\n\n1. IDENTIFICATION. Neon58's 16-variable quotient is a unate-split CNF N\u2227P (N all-negative, P all-positive) with cross-intersection (CI): every N-clause shares a variable with every P-clause. Lemma D (elementary, unchecked): such F is UNSAT iff every minimal transversal of P's hypergraph is exactly the variable set of an N-clause. So SAT on this class is polynomially equivalent to monotone dualization. (a) Fredman-Khachiyan 1996 (recalled, not re-verified) gives quasi-polynomial time. (b) A polynomial all-work theorem for this class with arbitrary CI-preserving extras would put dualization in P, which is open to my knowledge. The honest target is quasi-polynomial.\n\n2. MECHANISM FK-ORDER (unimplemented; per-state adaptive worklist instead of one global order).\n(i) Weight test, sound for any CNF: if w = sum of 2^-|C| is below 1, the state is SAT, with a witness by conditional expectations.\n(ii) Otherwise some clause C* has |C*| <= log2 m. By CI every opposite-side clause meets C*, so some v in C* occurs in at least |O|/log2 m opposite clauses. Branch on v; canonicalise by UP, stripping propagated units and absent variables; memoise canonical states.\nInvariants: restriction and UP preserve unate-split and CI, because a crossing pair that loses its only shared variable has one member satisfied. With V=|N||P|, one child has V' <= (1-1/log2 m)V and the other V' <= V-1; V=0 means one side is empty, hence SAT. So T(V) <= T((1-eps)V)+T(V-1)+1, giving m^O(log^2 m) nodes. The bound needs no IALH, DP or subsumption.\nWork: O(L) literal visits per node plus an exact dyadic sum of at most w_max+log m bits; total m^O(log^2 m) * L log n bit operations. The search tree is itself a tree-like resolution refutation of that size, so the certificate costs no more than the search.\nMonitor: at every UNSAT CI node the best opposite-side frequency fraction phi of the shortest clause is at least 1/log2 m. A logged node with w>=1 and smaller phi proves the residual left the class and names the non-crossing pairs.\nIndependent-test prediction: on Neon58's quotient, with ties broken by frequency among shortest clauses and then smallest index, FK-ORDER visits at most 12 distinct non-terminal canonical states (my trace: 9) and at most 24 restrictions; on the k-pair family at most 3k+1 states.\n\n3. SOUND RESTRICTED FACTORING (arbitrary extras allowed). DUAL-FACTOR: if a set N0 of all-negative input clauses equals the set of minimal vertex covers of a graph H on its variables, then N0 is equivalent to OR over edges {u,v} of (not u AND not v) and may be replaced by a selector encoding. Check: enumerate minimal vertex covers with polynomial delay, stopping after |N0|+1 outputs. This is an equivalence of a clause subset, so other clauses are unconstrained. Neon58: 2*2^k clauses become 4k+2. It covers overlapping groups, which the rectangle rule did not. Choosing N0 among extras is heuristic.\n\n4. EXTRAS AND ARBITRARY CNF. A UNSAT-only CI-core probe in the style of the v5 core: peel clauses with the most non-crossing partners until CI holds, run FK-ORDER under a node budget, accept only UNSAT. Polarity doubling makes any CNF unate-split with N a matching, and CI then holds iff every clause mentions every variable. The CI defect is therefore the exact obstruction. Provable: a strong backdoor of size b into the class gives 2^b times quasi-polynomial, since the class is restriction-closed.\n\n5. AUDIT. Compression verifier: blocks are built from every clause, used forms are confined to the block mask, P*L=I is checked entrywise; I found no unsound skip. Core: subset gate, a certificate verified against the core, UNSAT only through 2-SAT. Cost findings: (a) windows() seeds only supports of width <= 5, so an input whose clauses all have width >= 6 gives IALH zero root windows; (b) elim accepts on clause count while widths grow, and each failed attempt canonicalises all p*q resolvents, about (pq)^2 subset tests, for every variable at every STUCK node; (c) step is memoised before canonicalisation.\n\n6. FIXTURE (control and obstruction witness, not a growth claim). f = maj3(maj3(1,2,3), maj3(4,5,6), M), M = maj3 of maj3 on 7..15; each of the 171 prime implicants appears as a positive and a negative clause: a self-dual, non-read-once dual pair. Claim A: every block has stabiliser {0,mask}, yet no certificate in the pinned format exists. A kernel vector must be constant on every block, hence all-ones, so all forms are even; blocks need 837 form-block incidences and 14 even forms supply at most 14*36=504. An overcomplete frame would need at least 24 coordinates for 15 variables. The skip is intrinsic, not a greedy artefact. Claim B (trace): compression skipped with incompatible_greedy_basis; core removes nothing; root IALH has no rows and DP is stuck; x1 leaves two incomparable states; at x2 every child collapses by DP alone to the 54-clause inner contradiction on 7..15 (clause counts 111,109,81,54 and 222,218,216,108,54); layers 3-6 hold one state; at x7 both children die by an empty UP table on window {10,11,13,14,15}. Untraced stress, no prediction: Fano composed with maj3, 21 variables, 378 width-6 clauses, zero root windows.",
  "missing_theorem": "MT1 (known in the literature as I recall it; needs an independent, Lean-sized proof in this CNF form): Lemma D; preservation of unate-split and CI under restriction and UP; the weight test; the m^O(log^2 m) node bound for FK-ORDER.\n\nMT2 (open problem, not a gap I can close): a polynomial total-work bound on CI unate-split CNF is equivalent to polynomial-time monotone dualization.\n\nMT3 (what arbitrary CNF needs; unproved): a restriction-monotone, polynomially computable defect d(F) vanishing on the class, with total work at most poly(L) * 2^O(d) * m^O(log^2 m), plus a polynomial procedure producing a defect witness. I can prove only the backdoor version, where finding the backdoor costs n^b. Monotone-split SAT without CI is NP-complete, so d cannot be uniformly small.\n\nMT4: DUAL-FACTOR for hypergraph rank r>2 with a polynomial verification bound (I recall incremental-polynomial enumeration for bounded rank but have not checked the statement), and any guarantee for choosing N0 under extra clauses.\n\nMT5 (restricted, about the pinned code): for which fan-ins does clause-count-nonincreasing DP collapse nested-majority dual pairs? The fixture margins are 4 and 2 clauses. I conjecture failure at inner fan-in 5, without proof.",
  "self_attack": "1. The Fredman-Khachiyan statement and bound are recalled from memory. My recurrence sketch may hide a gap, for example in using the original m for eps in subproblems.\n2. Quasi-polynomial is not polynomial. On the pair-transversal family the v5 frontier is already polynomial in encoded size, and last round's lookahead order also repairs Neon58. FK-ORDER adds a proof-backed rule and monitor, not a demonstrated speedup.\n3. Fixture risks. IALH may refute a layer-1 state through a lattice row I missed, giving peak 1. The DP margins 218<=222 and 216<=218 are hand counts; if the reduction of the A=x3 state is wrong, layer 3 could hold three states. Runtime may exceed 20 seconds: about ten IALH calls and roughly 6000 UP tuples on up to 342 clauses. A typo among 342 hand-written clauses would invalidate everything, possibly making the formula satisfiable.\n4. The fixture shows v5 succeeding. It is evidence that an incompatible skip can be intrinsic and that DP factoring is fragile, not a hard instance. The Fano stress is untraced.\n5. CI-core peeling can destroy unsatisfiability; choosing a good crossing subfamily is a biclique-type problem with no guarantee.\n6. The doubling argument shows generic CNF is maximally far from CI. Nothing here approaches all-CNF, kernel-free pigeonhole included; pigeonhole is unate-split but not CI.\n7. DUAL-FACTOR at rank 2 overlaps earlier selector proposals; only the verification method and the overlapping-group scope are new.\n8. The audit cost findings are read from the code and unmeasured.",
  "mechanism_signature": "FK-ORDER: Neon58's class = cross-intersecting unate-split CNF = monotone dualization. Weight test plus shortest-clause/opposite-frequency branching with a quasi-polynomial volume recurrence; phi monitor for leaving the class; DUAL-FACTOR graph-dual selector rule with polynomial-delay verification; UNSAT-only CI-core probe; kernel-constant incidence bound proving that no adapted basis or small frame exists; 15-variable self-dual nested-majority control.",
  "delta_from_prior": "00067 repaired Neon58 by lookahead ordering and cofactor classes, 00066 by rectangle definitions; neither had a class-level work bound. New here: an exact identification with monotone dualization, which makes a polynomial bound on this class a named open problem and a quasi-polynomial one provable; a lookahead-free branching rule with a volume invariant and a runtime monitor; a factoring rule verified by output-sensitive enumeration that covers overlapping groups; a proof that an incompatible-greedy skip can be intrinsic; and three code-level cost findings (width-6 window blindness, quartic failed DP attempts, clause-count acceptance with width growth).",
